//                   ADR-231 D6 (fail-closed gateway egress gate + O+ kill-switch)
// Story           : CHO-2148
//
// Owning domain : Tenancy + Billing (chora_tenancy database)
// Owning team   : Team 3 (Platform)
// Topic prefix  : chora.tenancy.external_egress_policy.*
//
// WHY THIS EVENT EXISTS — it is the ONLY bridge between two databases.
//
// chora-tenancy owns the external-egress entitlement (deterministic tenant
// administration; the Tenant Admin sets it in H+). The model-gateway, however,
// must consult it fail-closed on EVERY grounded-search call, and it reads from
// chora_observability.external_egress_policy — a different database.
//
// Cross-DB queries and writes are FORBIDDEN (13-DB topology,
// .claude/rules/ddd-enforcement.md), so chora-tenancy CANNOT write that table.
// It publishes this event instead, and a chora-observability subscriber projects
// it into the read-copy. Break this event and the gateway silently keeps serving
// a stale entitlement — which is why the projection carries `version` (below).
//
// SAFETY POSTURE — default-deny. A tenant with NO row in either database is OFF.
// Franchise tenants (schools, minors) therefore need no seeding: absence IS the
// denial. This event never needs to be published to keep a tenant OFF.
//
// EVERY event message embeds chora.common.v1.EventEnvelope as field 1.
